> _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:183:## Phase 4 — Partial runs & resilience
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:184:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:185:### 4.1 Remaining run modes
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:186:Selected-nodes+deps, from-node-through-descendants, 
retry-failed, retry-failed+descendants. Scope calculation in `validation.py`/`scheduler.py`; toolbar + context-menu 
entries.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:187:**Done when:** pytest covers subgraph scope for each 
mode on branch/diamond graphs; UI can run any mode.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:188:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:189:### 4.2 Fingerprints, cache reuse, stale propagation
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:190:`cache.py`: canonical fingerprint (type+version, 
relevant config, upstream artifact fingerprints, adapter schema version). Reuse only on fingerprint match + artifacts 
exist + integrity check + prior success + no forced regen. Edge/config/upstream changes mark descendants stale 
(orange). Persist cache-hit/miss reasons.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:191:**Done when:** re-running an unchanged workflow 
re-executes zero nodes; changing one upstream config re-executes exactly the affected subgraph (pytest-proven).
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:192:Also in this step: **Result Viewer pinning** — an 
edited viewer payload becomes a winning cache entry (validated against the port type) that feeds downstream nodes 
until unpinned, and editing it marks descendants stale; pinned state is visible on the stub card.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:193:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:194:### 4.3 Retry policies + explicit error outputs
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:195:Per-node `on_error`: stop / bounded retry with 
delay/backoff / continue via explicit error output (control path) / skip-optional — only where capability flags 
permit. Structured failure payloads (stable code, user message, redacted details, attempt, recovery suggestion).
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:196:**Done when:** pytest covers each policy including 
backoff timing and error-branch routing.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:197:
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:198:### 4.4 Run history + deep inspection UI
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:199:Bottom panel full version: execution list (`GET 
/api/workflow/executions?workflow_id=`), node timeline, per-node resolved inputs/outputs/logs/errors/attempts, cache 
decisions and stale reasons. Summaries by default, explicit expansion for large values.
  _dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan.md:200:**Done when (Phase 4 gate):** a failed run can be 
diagnosed and retried from the UI without rerunning successful nodes.
